<title>USA: NYSE suspends Duty Free, seeks to delist.</title>
<headline>NYSE suspends Duty Free, seeks to delist.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Wednesday it suspended trading in the common stock of Duty Free International, and it will apply to delist the company.</p>
<p>The NYSE said the move is a result of a tender offer by BAA Plc that expired Tuesday. Duty Free now has fewer than 600,000 common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The NYSE said it normally considers suspending and removing from its list companies which have fewer than 600,000 common shares held by the public.</p>
</text>
